{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1457535","title":"Dynamics of Enterobacteriaceae reservoirs harboring blaCTX-M group 1 in community wastewater systems","description":"The rising prevalence of clinically significant blaCTX-M group 1 resistance genes in human populations underscores the need for further investigation, particularly to elucidate the establishment and dynamics of environmental reservoirs. In this study, we combined molecular and culture-based approaches to examine the potential origins, abundance, and temporal dynamics of blaCTX-M group 1 genes in wastewater systems. We sequenced blaCTX-M amplicons from 14 wastewater raw influent samples to identify abundant variants and their enzyme groups in wastewater. We performed whole-genome sequencing for 24 selectively isolated Escherichia coli strains to assess their antibiotic resistance, particularly the presence of the blaCTX-M gene, and virulence gene profiles. Our results revealed a high prevalence of blaCTX-M group 1 genes among wastewater E. coli, with resistance and virulence profiles closely resembling those observed in clinical isolates, highlighting the importance of monitoring antibiotic resistance in wastewater systems.","center":"University of Wisconsin-Milwaukee","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2026/04/24 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN57465268","MIGS Cultured Bacterial/Archaeal sample from Escherichia coli","uncertain",null,null,2020,"US","Wisconsin",5263045,"Milwaukee","verified",null,null,"USA: Milwaukee",null,"wastewater","Jones Island and South Shore","raw inflluent","conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical"],["SAMN57465269","MIGS Cultured Bacterial/Archaeal sample from Escherichia coli","uncertain",null,null,2